% -e over a query answered through its Magic rewrite, where the query binds
% its call through another literal rather than a constant: the seed is then a
% rule reading start/1 rather than a fact.  ready/0 is called with no column
% to bind, so its adornment has no magic predicate and no guard.

start(a).
edge(a, b).
edge(b, c).
edge(x, y).

ready :- edge(a, b).

path(X, Y) :- ready, edge(X, Y).
path(X, Z) :- edge(X, Y), path(Y, Z).

start(S), path(S, X)?
